From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Osterloh <richard.osterloh@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:29:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] task_wdt: forget a hardware watchdog that rejected its config

task_wdt_init() kept hw_wdt_dev when wdt_install_timeout() failed, so a
later task_wdt_init(NULL) still ran wdt_setup() and wdt_feed() on a
watchdog with no timeout installed. Clear it on the error path so the
documented software-only fallback can be retried.

Signed-off-by: Richard Osterloh <richard.osterloh@gmail.com>
---
 subsys/task_wdt/task_wdt.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/subsys/task_wdt/task_wdt.c b/subsys/task_wdt/task_wdt.c
index a7741f966..87b3449d1 100644
--- a/subsys/task_wdt/task_wdt.c
+++ b/subsys/task_wdt/task_wdt.c
@@ -142,6 +142,7 @@ int task_wdt_init(const struct device *hw_wdt)
 		hw_wdt_channel = wdt_install_timeout(hw_wdt_dev, &wdt_config);
 		if (hw_wdt_channel < 0) {
 			LOG_ERR("hw_wdt install timeout failed: %d", hw_wdt_channel);
+			hw_wdt_dev = NULL;
 			return hw_wdt_channel;
 		}
 #else
